      "key": [
        "Callas the Unfaithful",
        "Callas' case",
        "Callas's case"
      ],
      "keysecondary": [],
      "comment": "Callas: Callas the Unfaithful",
      "content": "The nickname Poisson gave Callas after he was arrested over Jacques's death at a banquet. Benefactors withdrew support and the epithet outlived him for years, so a statue of him would have been too controversial. Navia, the Spina and old friends such as Florent refused to use it. Navia cleared his name at the Chapter IV trial.",
